{"ld": 1228, "paper": "HP803", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Clarify Certain Terms in and to Make Other Changes to the Automotive Right to Repair Laws (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-roberts-lovell-tiffany", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-collamore-amanda", "h-crockett-edward", "h-golek-cheryl", "s-guerin-stacey", "h-mingo-arthur", "s-rafferty-joseph", "h-walker-mark"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This bill adds and clarifies definitions for terms contained within the automotive right to repair laws enacted by Initiated Bill 2023, chapter 3.\n\nThe bill reduces the applicability of the automotive right to repair laws to a narrower class of vehicles. Under the bill, motor vehicles subject to the right to repair provisions enacted by Initiated Bill 2023, chapter 3 are self-propelled vehicles, not exclusively operated on railroad tracks, that have a seating capacity of not more than 15 persons, including the operator. The bill specifies that the following types of vehicles are not subject to the provisions enacted by Initiated Bill 2023, chapter 3: vehicles used primarily for commercial purposes; motorcycles; snowmobiles; all-terrain vehicles and motorized wheelchairs, electric personal assistive mobility devices or electric bicycles.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0803&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "vetoed", "status_label": "Veto Sustained", "final_disposition": {"label": "Veto Sustained", "date": "2026-01-20", "governor_action": "Veto", "governor_action_date": "2026-01-07"}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1228)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0803&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-764)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0803&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}, {"label": "Amendment C-B (H-765)",